                    "What is 3D rendering?",
                    "3D rendering is where we produce a photorealistic image or video of a 3D model. Software can add textures to it, a degree of lighting, plus minute details to complete the vision, which will look very real; almost photorealistic. Often used to visualize what an object, a space, or a building will look like before it is even built so that sales can take place in advance."
                ],
                [
                    "Is 3D rendering difficult?",
                    "The software isn’t easy, and achieving photorealism requires quite a bit of work and skill, mostly involving lighting, materials, etc where a lot of renders often fall or rise. It is not something most businesses do in-house, which is why they work with a rendering team rather than buying and learning the software themselves."
                ],
                [
                    "Will AI replace 3D rendering?",
                    "AI can speed up some of the work; it is helpful for early concepts and early visual ideas, but to show the authentic product and match with your brand accurately requires a physical model, proper materials, and judgement.AI cannot provide a real picture guarantee yet for accurately portraying the real model product."
                ],
                [
                    "What software is best for 3D rendering?",
                    "They’re varied depending on the job, but the professional standards are V-Ray and Corona for photorealism and Blender and 3ds Max for the Modelling/scene setup, and like with anything, it is much more to do with the person using the software than the software they are using to be able to get excellent results from the same engine."
                ],
                [
                    "Why should you use 3D rendering for your business?",
                    "Because it lets you show and sell something before it exists. Market the product before it has been made; show alternatives in colour & finishes without using real samples; clearly show to your customer or client exactly what to expect and attractively; reduce turnaround time of decisions; achieve pre-sales; and avoid the high cost of making changes once a product has been made."
                ],
